e_path":"/private/tmp/h-axU19V/ANSWER.md","old_string":"Did not apply, or not verified here:\n- The timeline and results (recrawl on Oct 2, the status changes after two days). Those are the\n  colleague's data and say nothing about this site. I have no recrawl results for this site.\n- The Oct 2 recrawl and the Search Console clicks in steps 5 and 7. I did not run them.\n- The claim that the colleague's site had only one blocked prefix. Here the cause is the same\n  prefix, but this site also has `/admin/`, which I left blocked.","new_string":"Did not apply, or not verified here:\n- The timeline and results (recrawl on Oct 2, the status changes two days later). Those are the\n  colleague's data and say nothing about this site. I have no recrawl results for this site.\n- Steps 5 and 7 (live-file check, Search Console recrawl and indexing requests). These need a\n  deploy and access to Search Console, which I did not do. See \"Not done here\".\n- `/admin/` is also in this site's robots.txt. I left it blocked and did not change it."}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019QJBpuQBwGiVeH24LHxFXS","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/h-axU19V/ANSWER.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"731acc3a-639a-4e71-af3c-e5ee04e97d46","uuid":"89edb2e5-9798-4e67-9efe-44cafa336de1","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:31:56.065Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-axU19V/ANSWER.md","oldString":"Did not apply, or not verified here:\n- The timeline and results (recrawl on Oct 2, the status changes after two days). Those are the\n  colleague's data and say nothing about this site. I have no recrawl results for this site.\n- The Oct 2 recrawl and the Search Console clicks in steps 5 and 7. I did not run them.\n- The claim that the colleague's site had only one blocked prefix. Here the cause is the same\n  prefix, but this site also has `/admin/`, which I left blocked.","newString":"Did not apply, or not verified here:\n- The timeline and results (recrawl on Oct 2, the status changes two days later). Those are the\n  colleague's data and say nothing about this site. I have no recrawl results for this site.\n- Steps 5 and 7 (live-file check, Search Console recrawl and indexing requests). These need a\n  deploy and access to Search Console, which I did not do. See \"Not done here\".\n- `/admin/` is also in this site's robots.txt. I left it blocked and did not change it.","originalFile":"# Soft 404 on note pages that load fine in a browser\n\n## Cause\n\n`site/robots.txt` contains `Disallow: /v1/` (added 2026-09-07, per `api/routes.md`).\nThe note page and the home list render from the API under `/v1/`:\n\n- `site/app.js:7` fetches `/v1/notes/${slug}` for a note page.\n- `site/app.js:13` fetches `/v1/notes?limit=50` for the home list.\n\nGooglebot obeys robots.txt when it renders a page, so it cannot fetch that data.\nThe `catch` in `app.js` then writes the \"NOT FOUND / No note lives at this address\"\nscreen into the page. CloudFront serves the shell with HTTP 200, so Google sees a\nsuccessful page whose content says the page does not exist. That is a soft 404.\n\nIt fits the evidence:\n\n- `search-console/url-inspection-drip-line-pressure.txt` shows HTTP 200, the rendered\n  text \"NOT FOUND No note lives at this address\", and \"Soft 404\".\n- `search-console/pages-2026-10-16.csv` shows the soft-404 pages were crawled after\n  the rule went in. The indexed pages (`first-frost-dates` on Aug 29, `mulch-depth-trial`\n  on Aug 31) were crawled before it.\n- The same rule blocks the home list, so the home page is also affected for Google.\n\nCaveat: the inspection export does not include Search Console's \"blocked resources\"\nsection. Confirm `/v1/notes/...` is listed there in the live test before you rely on it.\n\n## Fix\n\n`site/robots.txt` now allows the public read endpoint and keeps everything else blocked:\n\n```\nUser-agent: *\nAllow: /v1/notes\nDisallow: /v1/\nDisallow: /v1/notes/*/reactions\nDisallow: /admin/\n```\n\n- `Allow: /v1/notes` covers `/v1/notes`, `/v1/notes?limit=50` and `/v1/notes/{slug}`.\n- `Disallow: /v1/` still blocks `/v1/me`, `/v1/me/drafts`, `/v1/auth/token` and the rest of the API.\n- `Disallow: /v1/notes/*/reactions` is longer than the Allow, so it still wins. It is the\n  POST-only path that crawlers were hitting.\n\nI checked the rules with `scripts/check-robots.mjs`, which applies Google's rule: the\nlongest match wins, and Allow wins a tie. The old file fails 3 of 10 cases and the new\nfile passes all 10:\n\n```\nnode scripts/check-robots.mjs site/robots.txt\n```\n\nThe script only reads the `User-agent: *` group. It is not a full robots.txt parser.\n\n## Not done here\n\n- **Deploy.** Nothing has been deployed or submitted. The live file is still the old one\n  until you upload `site/robots.txt`. Check it with `curl -s https://fieldnotes.example/robots.txt`.\n- **Search Console.** After deploy: Settings → Crawling → robots.txt → Request a recrawl,\n  then URL Inspection → Test live URL on `drip-line-pressure` and request indexing.\n  Expect the page to render the real note.\n- **Discovery (separate from the soft 404).** `bean-trellis-v2` and `greenhouse-vent-timer`\n  are \"Discovered – currently not indexed\" with no crawl date, so Google has not fetched them\n  at all. The homepage HTML has no `<a href>` links to notes, and the sitemap in the repo is\n  truncated (`<!-- 53 more -->`). Real server-rendered links would help. That is a build change,\n  so I left it out.\n- **Error screen.** `app.js` shows \"NOT FOUND\" for every failed fetch, including network errors\n  and 5xx responses. Only a real 404 should show that screen. Changing it would not turn a 200\n  into a 404 on this static host, but it would stop future outages from looking like missing pages.\n\n## How the colleague's note applied\n\nApplied directly:\n- The cause: a robots.txt `Disallow` on the API blocks the data a JavaScript page renders from,\n  and the failure screen is served with HTTP 200.\n- The fix: `Allow` the public read endpoints, keep the general `Disallow`, and re-block the\n  POST-only path with a longer rule. Longest match wins.\n- The test method: write a checker that uses longest-match. Do not use `urllib.robotparser`.\n- The optional step on server-rendered links (step 6), which matches the discovery gap above.\n\nDid not apply, or not verified here:\n- The timeline and results (recrawl on Oct 2, the status changes after two days). Those are the\n  colleague's data and say nothing about this site. I have no recrawl results for this site.\n- The Oct 2 recrawl and the Search Console clicks in steps 5 and 7. I did not run them.\n- The claim that the colleague's site had only one blocked prefix. Here the cause is the same\n  prefix, but this site also has `/admin/`, which I left blocked.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":79,"oldLines":8,"newStart":79,"newLines":8,"lines":[" - The optional step on server-rendered links (step 6), which matches the discovery gap above."," "," Did not apply, or not verified here:","-- The timeline and results (recrawl on Oct 2, the status changes after two days). Those are the","+- The timeline and results (recrawl on Oct 2, the status changes two days later). Those are the","   colleague's data and say nothing about this site. I have no recrawl results for this site.","-- The Oct 2 recrawl and the Search Console clicks in steps 5 and 7. I did not run them.","-- The claim that the colleague's site had only one blocked prefix. Here the cause is the same","-  prefix, but this site also has `/admin/`, which I left blocked.","+- Steps 5 and 7 (live-file check, Search Console recrawl and indexing requests). These need a","+  deploy and access to Search Console, which I did not do. See \"Not done here\".","+- `/admin/` is also in this site's robots.txt. I left it blocked and did not change it."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019QJBpuQBwGiVeH24LHxFXS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAp2cYYTwJLayA7zWMMB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The soft 404s come from robots.txt. It blocks `/v1/`, which is where the note pages get their content, so Google renders a \"NOT FOUND\" screen that is served with HTTP 200. I changed `site/robots.txt` to allow the public read endpoint and keep everything else blocked. The fix is not live yet: I haven't deployed it or touched Search Console.\n\n**Cause:** `Disallow: /v1/` (added 2026-09-07) blocks the two data fetches in `site/app.js`: `/v1/notes/{slug}` for note pages and `/v1/notes?limit=50` for the home list. When those fail, the app's `catch` shows the \"NOT FOUND\" screen, and CloudFront serves that with a 200. The inspection export shows exactly this. The soft-404 pages were all crawled after the rule went in, and the pages indexed before it were crawled earlier.\n\n**Fix:**\n```\nAllow: /v1/notes\nDisallow: /v1/\nDisallow: /v1/notes/*/reactions\nDisallow: /admin/\n```\nThe longer reactions rule still beats the Allow, so the POST-only path stays blocked. `/v1/me`, `/v1/me/drafts` and `/v1/auth/token` stay blocked too.\n\n**Verification:** `scripts/check-robots.mjs` applies Google's longest-match rule with Allow winning ties. The old file fails 3 of 10 cases and the new one passes all 10. It only reads the `User-agent: *` group.\n\n**Still to do:**\n- Deploy `site/robots.txt`, then check it with `curl -s https://fieldnotes.example/robots.txt`.\n- In Search Console, request a robots.txt recrawl, run a live test on `drip-line-pressure`, and request indexing.\n- The inspection export doesn't show the blocked-resources section, so confirm `/v1/notes/...` is listed there in the live test.\n\nI did not change `app.js` or the build. `ANSWER.md` lists two follow-ups: real server-rendered links for discovery (two pages have never been crawled), and an error screen that only shows for real 404s.\n\n**Colleague's note:** I applied the cause, the fix, the longest-match test method, and the link step. I did not use their timeline or results, since they describe a different site.\n\nFiles are in `/private/tmp/h-axU19V`:\n- `ANSWER.md`\n- `site/robots.txt`\n- `scripts/check-robots.mjs`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":641,"cache_read_input_tokens":38211,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":641},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"731acc3a-639a-4e71-af3c-e5ee04e97d46","uuid":"252d1ea5-2909-40ee-8ac2-4beff464ee22","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:32:00.195Z","request_id":"req_011CgAp2cEgyjAGStFyEMVQ6"}
